#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128873 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129106 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "82f5682f-73b8-5c0a-b7d3-3336200843a0" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Roots of a Function Given Its Graph"}] :question/id #uuid "c1e36290-8271-5508-9bf8-cf15a3907f75" :question/math-academy-id "e-14174" :question/problem "What are the roots of the function shown below?\n\n![](images/ee/eef552d392c76e2a980a443faba33ffb8edda502aa31fb078374a6445365d242.png)" :question/worked-solution "The roots of the function are the $x$-intercepts. Therefore, the roots are\n\n$$\nx=-6,-3,0,3,6\n$$\n\n![](images/53/534bffb28abfa0609ae498f987be560f82037134e21d16e79c133ed82f1b1cd3.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128874 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129107 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "02e29602-b3c0-5ceb-ab65-710c06a08c1d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Roots of a Function Given a Table"}] :question/id #uuid "a443151c-f310-533e-adb7-1c8eda168738" :question/math-academy-id "e-14176" :question/problem "If $f(x)$ is given by the table shown below, what are its roots?\n\n| $x$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $f(x)$ | $5$ | $0$ | $-2$ | $-4$ | $0$ | $1$ | $3$ |" :question/worked-solution "The roots of the function are the values of $x$ such that\n\n$$\nf(x)=0\n$$\n\nIn the given table, we see that\n\n$$\nf(-2)=0\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nf(1)=0\n$$\n\nTherefore, the roots of the function are $x=-2$ and $x=1$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128875 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129108 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "578132af-f322-5a68-9771-72e1954622ad" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Roots of a Function Given a Mapping Diagram"}] :question/id #uuid "c92eb920-7734-57fd-9f34-c1917d435eaf" :question/math-academy-id "e-14177" :question/problem "What are the roots of the function $g(x)$ defined by the mapping diagram shown below?\n\n![](images/95/951e37aa910fa9cf3588ee047dd6258f8e628198ce3ce4620119d4b30bee8c8d.png)" :question/worked-solution "The roots of the function are the values of $x$ such that $g(x)=0$. In the given mapping diagram, we see that $g(9) = 0$.\n\nTherefore, the only root of the function is $x=9$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128876 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129109 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "82d522a8-ae3c-5723-909e-540ddac1d9da" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Roots Given a Function Definition"}] :question/id #uuid "d5e99647-7ada-562f-8a16-a61f4d1ae0be" :question/math-academy-id "e-14179" :question/problem "What is the root of the function $f(x)=2-4x$?" :question/worked-solution "The roots are the solutions to the equation\n\n$$\nf(x)=0\n$$\n\nwhich we solve as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x) &= 0 \\\\\n2 - 4x &= 0 \\\\\n4x &= 2 \\\\\nx &= \\frac{1}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function has the single root\n\n$$\nx=\\dfrac12\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129649 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129107 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "02e29602-b3c0-5ceb-ab65-710c06a08c1d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Roots of a Function Given a Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ac2bfd91-018a-5ad9-bf24-a7080a991245" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-2$ and $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127376} {:answer/id #uuid "3c361c6b-4d38-5f75-bcfd-c88f32f4a66c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-3$ and $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127377} {:answer/id #uuid "56828c6d-c656-5244-a6fb-07a7a9720948" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-3$ and $5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127378} {:answer/id #uuid "5b29cd8f-68ea-54c5-a37d-327d53ae87a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0$ a